Q) Companies often perform salary analyses to ensure fair compensation practices. One useful analysis is to check if there are any employees earning more than their direct managers.

As a HR Analyst, you're asked to identify all employees who earn more than their direct managers. The result should include the employee's ID and name.

A)
SELECT em_table.employee_id, em_table.name
FROM employee em_table
INNER JOIN employee manager_join
ON em_table.manager_id = manager_join.employee_id 
WHERE em_table.salary > manager_join.salary
;
